Subject: [DRAFT] Pong scanout: pin the wire offsets, not just the sizes

Draft only. Not in any series, not built, not applied.

sizeof() alone cannot hold a layout: swap two uint64_t members and every size
assertion above stays green while both readers silently read the wrong field.
These assertions pin the offsets the two readers actually depend on, and the
four method codes a presenter switches on.

Zero runtime change, zero structure change. Adopt together with the presenter
half (pong-presenter-assert-offsets.patch): the same facts asserted on both
sides break the build that broke the contract, with a message that names it.

--- a/drivers/PongAdreno/PongScanoutWire.h
+++ b/drivers/PongAdreno/PongScanoutWire.h
@@ -13,3 +13,24 @@
 struct PongScanoutDone {uint64_t sequence;uint32_t status,reserved;};
 static_assert(sizeof(PongScanoutModeInfo)==40 && sizeof(PongScanoutWaitInfo)==8 &&
     sizeof(PongScanoutFrame)==48 && sizeof(PongScanoutDone)==16,"Pong scanout wire");
+/* Where each field lands, for the two readers that index them:
+ * PongAdrenoScanout.cpp writes Frame@149 and validates Done@122, and
+ * PongMetalScanout.h reads format and reserved out of the reply. A version
+ * bumped inside Frame.reserved@44 (see GPU-27-SCANOUT-WIRE-PROPOSAL.md)
+ * rides on these offsets staying put. */
+static_assert(offsetof(PongScanoutModeInfo,version)==0 && offsetof(PongScanoutModeInfo,format)==4 &&
+    offsetof(PongScanoutModeInfo,width)==8 && offsetof(PongScanoutModeInfo,height)==16 &&
+    offsetof(PongScanoutModeInfo,stride)==24 && offsetof(PongScanoutModeInfo,bytes)==32,
+    "Pong scanout mode layout");
+static_assert(offsetof(PongScanoutFrame,sequence)==0 && offsetof(PongScanoutFrame,address)==8 &&
+    offsetof(PongScanoutFrame,bytes)==16 && offsetof(PongScanoutFrame,stride)==24 &&
+    offsetof(PongScanoutFrame,width)==32 && offsetof(PongScanoutFrame,height)==36 &&
+    offsetof(PongScanoutFrame,format)==40 && offsetof(PongScanoutFrame,reserved)==44,
+    "Pong scanout frame layout");
+static_assert(offsetof(PongScanoutDone,status)==8 && offsetof(PongScanoutDone,reserved)==12,
+    "Pong scanout done layout");
+/* The presenter forwards these numbers unchanged (NativeAdrenoPublish.cpp:51-53),
+ * so the wire owns them: a renumbering here is an ABI break, not a rename. */
+static_assert(PongScanoutMode==0x7000 && PongScanoutWait==0x7002 &&
+    PongScanoutComplete==0x7003 && PongScanoutMemory==0x5343 && PongScanoutVersion==1 &&
+    PongScanoutBgra==1,"Pong scanout method codes");
